We're going to
find what questions

00:34:53.900 --> 00:34:56.900
might be online and come
back with those answers.

00:34:56.900 --> 00:34:57.530
Be right back.

00:36:26.930 --> 00:36:28.527
Great, and welcome back.

00:36:28.527 --> 00:36:30.360
So on the list here,
we have some questions.

00:36:30.360 --> 00:36:32.234
And we'll just go through
them one at a time.

00:36:32.234 --> 00:36:34.680
So the first question--
what's on the roadmap in terms

00:36:34.680 --> 00:36:37.830
of new infrastructure
hardware on Google Cloud?

00:36:37.830 --> 00:36:39.720
Well, it's a great question.

00:36:39.720 --> 00:36:42.030
In general, it's going to
be what the customers want.

00:36:42.030 --> 00:36:44.310
NVIDIA keeps releasing new GPUs.

00:36:44.310 --> 00:36:46.350
We just launched the V100.

00:36:46.350 --> 00:36:49.140
They made some announcements
of what might come next.

00:36:49.140 --> 00:36:51.150
There's always
interest on those.

00:36:51.150 --> 00:36:53.940
So as they launch
new high end GPUs,

00:36:53.940 --> 00:36:55.920
we'll probably be
bringing those in.

00:36:55.920 --> 00:36:57.960
And also just like
the cloud TPU,

00:36:57.960 --> 00:37:00.330
we focus on what
workloads are out there

00:37:00.330 --> 00:37:02.010
and what other
infrastructure hardware

00:37:02.010 --> 00:37:03.840
