00:37:03.840 --> 00:37:07.530
So as customers demand faster,
higher price performance

00:37:07.530 --> 00:37:09.300
ratios for
infrastructure, we'll look

00:37:09.300 --> 00:37:11.490
at new hardware accelerators.

00:37:11.490 --> 00:37:14.180
But just like GCE, it's not
just about those hardware

00:37:14.180 --> 00:37:15.150
accelerators.

00:37:15.150 --> 00:37:19.830
We'll also look at things like
what kind of CPU, memory, disc,

00:37:19.830 --> 00:37:20.454
network.

00:37:20.454 --> 00:37:21.870
And you can think
of Google always

00:37:21.870 --> 00:37:25.170
pushing forward on all of this.

00:37:25.170 --> 00:37:27.300
Second question--
what type of workloads

00:37:27.300 --> 00:37:30.120
are a good fit for the V100 GPU?

00:37:30.120 --> 00:37:31.120
Really, there's two.

00:37:31.120 --> 00:37:33.100
One is machine learning.

00:37:33.100 --> 00:37:35.760
Because of the mix precision
support and the NV Link

00:37:35.760 --> 00:37:37.830
connections between
the GPUs, this

00:37:37.830 --> 00:37:40.500
is a very optimal
machine learning GPU.

00:37:40.500 --> 00:37:42.990
A lot of our customers are
using these in large scale

00:37:42.990 --> 00:37:45.030
to do machine learning
training, starting

00:37:45.030 --> 00:37:47.830
to do some inference
workloads with Tensor RT.

00:37:47.830 --> 00:37:50.340
Great for ML, but also
just really good for high

00:37:50.340 --> 00:37:52.200
demanding HPC workloads.

00:37:52.200 --> 00:37:55.500
If you really want your
results done quickly and fast,

00:37:55.500 --> 00:37:58.870
it's a great GPU
for that as well.

00:37:58.870 --> 00:38:00.180
So the next question--

